From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 20:34:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01/73] chore(fork): add integration patch-management system on
 pinned upstream baseline
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Lifts the patches workflow used in gascity/gastown/beads, adapted for the
packs repo:

- integration branch = pinned BASELINE (upstream/main @ f69ec02b3) + fork
  patches; deliberately NOT a moving branch ref.
- make patches       — export BASELINE..HEAD divergence to patches/,
  excluding patches/ itself (no recursive self-inclusion).
- make upgrade       — reset integration to BASELINE and replay patches via
  git am --3way (scripts/upgrade-integration.sh); copies patches/ to a tmpdir
  before the reset since the baseline does not track it, then regenerates.
- make check-patches — fail if patches/ drifts from the divergence; wired into
  the integration-branch pre-push as validation-only (never amends).

Two deliberate departures from the gascity original, both documented:
BASELINE pins an upstream main SHA rather than a release tag (the newest tag
here is ~190 commits stale), and there is no BASELINE_VERSION because this
repo builds no binary to stamp.

Workflow: docs/fork-patches.md

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
